[quote="Foote"]

Megalopolis is not the place you want to start. There are so many *heros cant play cards* and *heros cant use powers* that it really disrupts learning the game if its your first time.&nbsp;

[/quote]

I can see that point; in fact, I got my backside handed to me by Omnitron in Megalopolis for my first game... but that really got me more excited to play it again and best them!! And thematically I felt it was a better debut mission for the heroes.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Fight the Ennead in the Tomb of Anubis.

&nbsp;

 :smiling_imp:

Welcome to the community!&nbsp;

&nbsp;

I would offer a few pointers on what to avoid for your first few games. Absolute Zero, Argent Adept, The Ennead, Megalopolis, and Nightmist. The heroes are a bit more complicated and would not be ideal for getting the basic rules down and getting a feel for the game in general. Megalopolis has a few cards that prevent you from playing parts of the game, and also is counter productive to learning the game. The Ennead are problably the most complicated villain to run (imo) as they have various triggers that could trigger more triggers, so again not good when you are trying to get started. All of those mentioned are fun and can be a delightful challenge, just not something for people trying to learn the basics. All of this is IMHO, of course.&nbsp;

